<article class="env-corollary" id="06DY">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06DY">Corollary <span data-tag="06DY">9.2.2.24</span>.</a> Let $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be a functor of $\infty $-categories, where $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is cocomplete. Then $F$ is cocontinuous if and only if it is finitely cocontinuous and finitary. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Apply Corollary <a data-tag="06DW" href="/tag/06DW">9.2.2.22</a> in the special case $\kappa = \aleph _0$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
